  "tagline": "Spotify's memory-mapped random-projection-tree ANN library; stable but no longer evolving.",
  "description": "Annoy is a C++ library with Python bindings that Spotify built for music recommendations. It builds forests of random projection trees into static, read-only files that are memory-mapped, so many processes can share one index with almost no load time. It supports Euclidean, Manhattan, cosine, Hamming and dot-product distances and can build on disk for data larger than RAM. The last release was 1.17.3 in June 2023 and Spotify's newer Voyager (HNSW) library is its practical successor, so Annoy is best treated as stable legacy.",
